-- title:
--   Good primes for finitely many rational matrices (`good_mats`)
-- statement:
--   Good primes for finitely many rational matrices: all denominators coprime to `q ^ f`.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.R6BitNBPrime`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem IntMul.Kappa.R6.Bit.NB.good_mats {ι κ : Type*} [Fintype ι] [Fintype κ] (S : Finset (Matrix ι κ ℚ)) :
--       ∃ q₀ : ℕ, ∀ q, q.Prime → q₀ < q → ∀ f : ℕ, ∀ A ∈ S, ∀ i j,
--         Nat.Coprime (A i j).den (q ^ f) ∧ (A i j ≠ 0 → IsUnit (redQ (q ^ f) (A i j)))
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Round six, bit network: good primes
--
--   Finitely many rationals have denominators coprime to every power of every prime `q > q₀`, and the
--   nonzero ones are units mod `q ^ f`. Consequently a finite set of edges with `EdgeQ` data
--   is `EdgeOK (q ^ f)` for all large primes `q` and all `f`.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** Part of the Lean formalization of the round-six κ-improvement (integer-multiplication-kappa campaign, target `IntMul.Kappa.jain_round6_framework`). The statement is copied verbatim from the Lean development; the platform node carries the same declaration name. Definitions it mentions live in the `IntMul_Kappa_R6_Defs*` bundles (on top of the published κ bundles `IntMul_Kappa_K_Defs*`).
